Hi Ed,
sorry for taking so long to reply to your quick response. You are correct this is a warning. However, the BRMSEA estimates do not converge with what I would expect from the Frequentist estimation. In fact the BRMSEA is consistently estimated to be zero:

> fitIDx.NonDec <- blavFitIndices(bfit.sem.NonDec, baseline.model = bfit.sem.NonDec.null)
Warning messages:
1: 43 (12.4%) p_waic estimates greater than 0.4. We recommend trying loo instead.
2: Some Pareto k diagnostic values are too high. See help('pareto-k-diagnostic') for details.
3: 26 (7.5%) p_waic estimates greater than 0.4. We recommend trying loo instead.
4: Some Pareto k diagnostic values are too high. See help('pareto-k-diagnostic') for details.
